comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-27T12:26:45.447Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: GH-1327 and all-status static inventory and Windows nightly searches found closed pm-lhhnx9 and older nightly lineages but no owner for this exact Windows assertion. Run 36310799887 log proves a distinct shard-2 failure."
  "2026-09-27T23:32:24.400Z","harness:codex","Verification: linked read-only inventory integration suite 9/9 passed, including a portable denied parent-stat negative control and unreadable parent-file classification. The integration file is now pinned to the required Windows Node 24 PR check. Full coverage passed 9380 tests at 100/100/100/100. Hosted Windows result remains pending."
  "2026-09-27T23:57:42.357Z","harness:codex",PR #1332 hosted coverage shard 1 failed because the workflow contract still expected the old Windows regression command. Updated its exact command assertion to include the static inventory suite already running and passing in required Windows regression; linked inventory and workflow-contract tests passed. Full coverage pending.
  "2026-09-28T00:38:11.104Z","harness:codex","Review verification: workflow contract 15/15 and Windows inventory 9/9 passed; required hosted Windows regression had already passed. Full static quality pipeline passed. Earlier full coverage was 100/100/100/100. Final rerun had two unrelated 30-second suite-load timeouts that passed in isolation; hosted coverage shards will validate this final head."
  "2026-09-28T02:34:52.541Z","harness:codex","Full Nightly Validation run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/36369419144 at exact head e3ad1955beba908a840748c4e96972a9f06ef8aa passed all seven jobs, including both Windows Node 24 shards, Ubuntu Node 22/24/25, macOS Node 24, and nightly quality. PR #1332 required Windows regression and Gates (coverage) also passed at run 36369408528. This completes the static inventory hosted acceptance."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-27T21:41:25.100Z","harness:codex",Hosted Nightly Validation run 36310799887 saw Windows report extensions_unreadable but omit managed_state_unreadable for a file in place of the managed-state parent directory. A parent stat now distinguishes missing state from an unreadable managed root.
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-27T21:41:27.107Z","harness:codex",Reading a child path below a non-directory parent can surface ENOENT on Windows instead of ENOTDIR. Classify absent managed state only after confirming the parent is a directory or genuinely absent.
